            {
                "entry_id": "518cdbf0-8982-3eab-92af-5ebcf94015b1",
                "word": "invertébré",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c8aabea9-7ab7-4fb4-ba8b-99fe44d2b9d3",
                        "entry_id": "518cdbf0-8982-3eab-92af-5ebcf94015b1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "invertébrés"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "14a9f82f-3866-3dcb-b114-a8c003796816",
                        "entry_id": "518cdbf0-8982-3eab-92af-5ebcf94015b1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Animal sans colonne vertébrale."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ellipsis"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "704d1362-5d43-44ef-8026-48524efbd0cd",
                                "sense_id": "14a9f82f-3866-3dcb-b114-a8c003796816",
                                "text": "Grand chasseur, le crapaud dévore toutes sortes de petits invertébrés, aptères ou ailés."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b229b294-ae00-4010-abd0-3c2b518c6135",
                                "sense_id": "14a9f82f-3866-3dcb-b114-a8c003796816",
                                "text": "Se pencher sur un limule est aussi une expérience un peu troublante... Souvent, l’invertébré se positionne pour mieux percevoir l'étranger. Dès lors, on ne sait plus très bien qui étudie qui."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1987abf9-1594-43b2-9ec1-e60ec6244802",
                                "sense_id": "14a9f82f-3866-3dcb-b114-a8c003796816",
                                "text": "Vous êtes plutôt des mollusques, des invertébrés, des protozoaires, des machins tout mous, sans squelette et sans coquilles, dégueulassement gluants et visqueux."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d5891199-b9f8-4b36-acc4-98574ee1db10",
                        "source_entry_id": "518cdbf0-8982-3eab-92af-5ebcf94015b1",
                        "source_sense_id": "14a9f82f-3866-3dcb-b114-a8c003796816",
                        "target_lang_word": "invertebrate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "invertebrate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3454f17b-13b4-3297-89e3-3a16ed9cfdb1",
                                        "entry_id": "f5e7a4c9-f1ec-356a-83aa-2e3c9f906bce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An animal without vertebrae, i.e. backbone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7d5998b-1789-4008-89cd-72983659d18e",
                                                "sense_id": "3454f17b-13b4-3297-89e3-3a16ed9cfdb1",
                                                "text": "Yet despite sounding inhospitable, grasslands such as this are home to a huge variety of smaller herbs and wildflowers, including some of the UK's rarest orchids and invertebrates, in addition to being home to butterfly species such as the Chalkhill Blue."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "06345511-8205-3e9b-8bf2-37eaec7148ad",
                                        "entry_id": "f5e7a4c9-f1ec-356a-83aa-2e3c9f906bce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A spineless person; a coward."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "invertebrate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66c01231-0668-3836-a943-6a40c73fbcce",
                                        "entry_id": "fa2de606-a598-3f22-b46d-7e05fb36f73b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lacking a backbone; without vertebrae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07995f7d-6f99-41e8-aae1-c6afb5709a33",
                                                "sense_id": "66c01231-0668-3836-a943-6a40c73fbcce",
                                                "text": "Tear it up, and put a fragment under the microscope, and, wonder of wonders! see the maze of geometric forms exhibited in the bones of the creature; for who can help regarding the spicules as bones, even though a sponge be invertebrate?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3dab811d-0e1c-30e4-9d1d-3ab58ce8a76e",
                                        "entry_id": "fa2de606-a598-3f22-b46d-7e05fb36f73b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cowardly, uncourageous; lacking character."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11b7b009-4ed2-440b-99fc-5309da596b70",
                                                "sense_id": "3dab811d-0e1c-30e4-9d1d-3ab58ce8a76e",
                                                "text": "This week Fifa’s morally invertebrate president, Gianni Infantino, gave a speech that attempted to paint his World Cup as a marker of a grand struggle between the bright new world and corrupt old Europe, with Infantino himself the Mandela at its centre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
